  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 106 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThe hot and mainly dry weather pattern persists heading into the \nweekend lasting through the forecast period. This is thanks to the \nupper ridge of high pressure positioned across the Great Basin to \nFour Corners region. Easterly to northeasterly flow aloft on the \nfringe of the high pressure will keep temperatures in the low to \nupper 90s for most locations. Meanwhile, areas along and near the \nriver valleys will top out in the low 100s. Daily low (10-20%) \nchances of isolated showers/storms are in store across the higher \nterrain and far West Texas due to upslope flow and shortwave \nimpulses rounding the periphery of the ridge. Most locations are \ngoing to remain dry. Low temperatures are expected to range from \nthe 60s to mid 70s regionwide each night. \n\nLamberson",
